      "rationale": "No third-party library reads or writes semio's own `.dsl.semio`/`.pack.semio` envelope, so a differential comparison's second PRODUCER cannot be a foreign package — it has to be a second implementation. `🧪️tests/mutate-semio-kit/🐍️component.py` is that implementation: the text envelope, the DSL grammar, the pack frame, the JSON projection and all fifteen verbs of `SemioKitMutation`, written in Python from the committed specification documents alone — `../🧬️schema/📸️snapshot/📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio` for the record grammar and its `h|c|s` pin tags, `…/📸️snapshot/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio` for the pack header and the sentence naming its six collections, `…/📸️snapshot/🔣️.json` for the projection, `…/🧬️schema/🧬️mutations/📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio` for the fifteen verbs and their argument lists, `🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/🧬️semio/🦀️.rs` for the semio envelope, and `ArtifactRef::to_uri` plus `LinkPin`/`BlobRef` for the dialect coordinate and the three pin shapes. It imports nothing from the Rust it judges and transliterates none of it. `package` is deliberately empty: the implementation is the adapter file, so this entry contributes no dependency to `🔒️dependencies.json` and nothing to the import-purity probe. The derivation of the pack layout past the header — which the protocol description names but declines to frame — is pinned by the Python re-encoding the committed `🎒️.pack.semio` byte for byte, which a misreading could not do.\n\nUNDER PROTOCOL V2 this registration is classified `cross-semio-implementation` — a required SUPPLEMENTAL oracle that does not discharge `semio-v1-kit-mutate`'s external-oracle requirement for its 15-kind mutation vocabulary; a qualifying third-party reference (`third-party-library` / `third-party-cli` / `standards-reference-tool`) is still owed.\n\n[2026-09-02, D1 — SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION] Promoted from cross-semio-implementation to verified-native-second-implementation: this artifact is semio-native (isSemioNativeArtifact), this reference's own third-party survey above (kept verbatim) already names what was checked and declined, its python implementation differs from the Rust subject, and it covers 100% of this manifest's 1 capability/capabilities with 15 committed fixture vector(s). See .🧬semio/🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️26/🌙️09/☀️02/SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION/📓️d1-native-oracle-discharge.md.",
